{"record":"deferral","spec":"133-document-final-gates","panel":"spec-133-final","slot":"R4","round":2,"finding":"ccr[0]","finding_sha256":"243a0263808604b0c2a7f0e0755738daf992b0a584460535b19a12c3e842cc1f","finding_text":"Property violated: R2.6 states the gate's purpose, that FinalizeEpic 'bring[s] no content into spec/\u003cid\u003e after the gate', and R2.4/R2.5 describe excluded-path content as the ledger and '.beads/issues.jsonl'. But the final_review subject drops every path under the Subject exclusions (internal/panel/subject.go: `Exclusions: []string{specs + \"/*/reviews/**\", \".mindspec/reviews/**\", \"review/**\", \".beads/issues.jsonl\"}`), and lifecycleSubjectDirt skips them (`if !panel.SubjectIncludes(name, roots) { continue }`). These globs admit any file, not only tool artifacts. Executed probe: after a passing final_review panel under enforce, a Go source file `review/evil.go` committed to spec/\u003cid\u003e, or left uncommitted in the spec worktree (FinalizeEpic's 'commit remaining spec artifacts' then commits it), passes impl approve with exit 0 and lands on main. The same for `.mindspec/reviews/evil.sh`. The control `evil.go` at the root is refused. In this repo `review/` is a tracked, non-ignored top-level directory that Go tooling builds and tests (`./...` does not skip it). So unreviewed code can land through impl approve by choosing an excluded path. Wrong implementation the ACs do not reject: the current one. Fix (build change): in the final_review gate of impl approve, refuse any path under an exclusion that differs between the reviewed head and the spec tip or the worktree, unless panel.IsToolArtifactPath(name, specDir) (`.beads/issues.jsonl`, `\u003cspecs\u003e/*/reviews/*/dispositions.jsonl`) or the path is git-ignored. Alternatively narrow the final_review exclusions to the tool-artifact set. Add a test where `review/x.go` committed after a passing final review makes impl approve refuse with the gate name before any write; it goes red on the current code (see this probe). If the gate holder judges this a pre-existing exclusion design (bead and spec gates share it), defer it to a filed bead rather than leave it unrecorded.","bead":"mindspec-zj35","by":"lane-orchestrator-spec-133-impl","created_at":"2026-10-25T10:36:36.835612Z"}
{"record":"disposition","id":"spec-133-final:R4:r2:ccr[0]:243a02638086:deferral","spec":"133-document-final-gates","gate":"final_review","panel":"spec-133-final","reviewer":"R4","model":"claude-opus-5-5","severity":"blocking","summary":"Property violated: R2.6 states the gate's purpose, that FinalizeEpic 'bring[s] no content into spec/\u003cid\u003e after the gate', and R2.4/R2.5 describe excluded-path content as the ledger and '.beads/issues.jsonl'. But the final_review subject drops every path under the Subject exclusions (internal/panel/subject.go: `Exclusions: []string{specs + \"/*/reviews/**\", \".mindspec/reviews/**\", \"review/**\", \".beads/issues.jsonl\"}`), and lifecycleSubjectDirt skips them (`if !panel.SubjectIncludes(name, roots) { continue }`). These globs admit any file, not only tool artifacts. Executed probe: after a passing final_review panel under enforce, a Go source file `review/evil.go` committed to spec/\u003cid\u003e, or left uncommitted in the spec worktree (FinalizeEpic's 'commit remaining spec artifacts' then commits it), passes impl approve with exit 0 and lands on main. The same for `.mindspec/reviews/evil.sh`. The control `evil.go` at the root is refused. In this repo `review/` is a tracked, non-ignored top-level directory that Go tooling builds and tests (`./...` does not skip it). So unreviewed code can land through impl approve by choosing an excluded path. Wrong implementation the ACs do not reject: the current one. Fix (build change): in the final_review gate of impl approve, refuse any path under an exclusion that differs between the reviewed head and the spec tip or the worktree, unless panel.IsToolArtifactPath(name, specDir) (`.beads/issues.jsonl`, `\u003cspecs\u003e/*/reviews/*/dispositions.jsonl`) or the path is git-ignored. Alternatively narrow the final_review exclusions to the tool-artifact set. Add a test where `review/x.go` committed after a passing final review makes impl approve refuse with the gate name before any write; it goes red on the current code (see this probe). If the gate holder judges this a pre-existing exclusion design (bead and spec gates share it), defer it to a filed bead rather than leave it unrecorded.","convergent_with":[],"disposition":"confirmed-deferred","evidence_ref":"mindspec-zj35","created_at":"2026-10-25T10:36:36.835612Z","round":2,"backfilled":false}
